WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:04.210
Huh? What's going on?

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:06.940
This is...

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:09.820
<i>This...</i>

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:16.840
Kan.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:20.750
Sae?!

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.410
What's going on here?

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.300
<b>Hand 12: 
Truth</b>

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.550
How did this happen?

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:36.530
Second Half
5th Players' Match

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:36.530
South Hand 3

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.680
<i>She called an open kan 
and discarded her draw?</i>

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.380
<i>She didn't do it to win 
or to further her hand?</i>

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:51.030
<i>Then maybe her reason for doing it 
was to increase the number of dora?</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.400
<i>Kan dora...</i>

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:01.210
<i>No, she's not after dora.</i>

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:03.140
<i>Kiyosumi's Miyanaga Saki almost never</i>

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:06.120
<i>adds more dora to her hand through kans.</i>

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:09.650
<i>In fact, I have two of the 
dora she created with that kan.</i>

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:13.380
<i>So her aim is most likely 
to change the drawing order.</i>

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:16.580
<i>If Kiyosumi's draw goes to Eisui,</i>

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:19.050
<i>and Eisui's draw goes to Miyamori,</i>

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.900
<i>Eisui and Miyamori's elimination 
of one suit will be stopped</i>

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.180
<i>and their hands will be slowed down temporarily.</i>

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.360
<i>Nothing will change for Kiyosumi and me, 
so we'll have the advantage.</i>

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.570
<i>So you're not scared of me, huh?</i>

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.070
<i>You really underestimate me.</i>

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.670
<i>Look at that, Kiyosumi!</i>

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:55.920
<i>That's what you get for underestimating me.</i>

00:01:58.690 --> 00:02:00.220
<i>Bring it on!</i>

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.360
<i>I'll let that go.</i>

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:20.360
<i>If I took that, it would be 7,700.</i>

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:24.540
<i>Should I have declared a riichi,
hoping for the reverse dora and ippatsu?</i>

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:29.420
<i>Nah, I don't want Miyamori 
chasing me down again.</i>

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.090
<i>Got it!</i>

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:43.680
Tsumo!

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.070
4,000. 8,000.

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:52.020
<i>Kiyosumi didn't win?</i>

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:59.740
<i>I want to say, "if only I had declared 
riichi," but I'd be too embarrassed.</i>

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.700
<i>With a ryanpeikou, it's a baiman tsumo.</i>

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.700
[Ryanpeikou - Two different iipeikou 
(double sequences) in one hand]

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.700
<i>She overtook us.</i>

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:10.180
<i>That's why you shouldn't count me out 
just because I don't have superpowers.</i>

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:11.830
<i>I'll defend second place with my life now.</i>

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:15.270
<i>I was in second place until East Hand 3.</i>

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:18.590
<i>Now, I need to get a baiman or 
haneman tsumo, or we'll be eliminated.</i>

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:25.760
<i>Everyone's festival would end.</i>

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:38.110
<i>I knew that I can't just change out a god 
once it's descended into me, but...</i>

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:44.920
I guess even a fast, cheap hand 
is too much to ask for right now.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:48.870
If only Haru or I could be 
there with her right now...

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.250
Too bad.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:51.910
It'll be all right.

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:54.630
Let's have faith in Kasumi-chan.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.880
<i>I'm not giving up yet.</i>

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:08.310
<i>I want to keep playing with 
everyone for as long as possible.</i>

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:11.680
<i>That's why I don't want to lose!</i>

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:16.230
Huh? Ei-chan?

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:17.680
Just now...

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:18.720
Toyone...

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:20.860
She's prioritizing speed.

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.180
That's dangerous in the second half...

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.610
She knows it too,

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:28.730
but she may have bet everything already on

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:30.620
this first half of the hand...

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:34.960
to continue this festival!

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:42.080
<i>We may be in second, but third place 
Eisui is only 100 points behind.</i>

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:45.880
<i>If Eisui wins a single hand, 
or if I play into anybody's hand,</i>

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:47.890
<i>we'll be eliminated.</i>

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:51.890
<i>I've got to keep an eye out for 
Eisui and cautiously step forward.</i>

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:51.080
<i>Now...</i>

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:55.890
<i>She had an extra bamboo tile.</i>

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:57.950
<i>Be there in time!</i>

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.800
<i>I need to finish this within the first half!</i>

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:08.280
<i>A one of circles?</i>

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:12.080
<i>Miyamori needs a direct hit 
baiman or a haneman tsumo.</i>

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:13.840
<i>Since she's also eliminated one suit,</i>

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:16.870
<i>her hand is probably all 
circles with some dora.</i>

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.420
<i>I can't discard any honor tiles.</i>

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:21.190
<i>Then,</i>

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:24.190
<i>this...</i>

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:25.070
Pon.

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.180
<i>Pon?</i>

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.740
<i>Not a kan?</i>

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:33.580
<i>Kiyosumi is making a move?!</i>

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:37.580
<i>As long as she doesn't deal into 
anyone's hand, she'd still win.</i>

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:39.960
<i>What the hell is she thinking?!</i>

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:52.220
<i>I need a draw, and here it is!</i>

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:07.960
Kan.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:21.440
Tsumo.

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:24.090
400. 800.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.760
That concludes game three 
of the second round match!

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:46.860
Thank you very much!

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:46.860
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
 Fifth Player - 3rd Year
 Anetai Toyone

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:50.050
Good game.

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.360
Eisui Girls' (Kagoshima)
 Fifth Player - 3rd Year
 Iwato Kasumi

00:07:54.230 --> 00:07:56.010
Thank you.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:57.370
Himematsu High School 
(South Osaka)
 Fifth Player - 3rd Year
 Suehara Kyouko

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.910
Thank you.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.210
Kiyosumi High School 
(Nagano)
 Fifth Player - 1st Year
 Miyanaga Saki

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:07.920
<b>The Nationals</b>

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:10.690
The schools proceeding to 
the semifinals will be

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:12.890
Kiyosumi High School from Nagano

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:15.890
and Himematsu High School from South Osaka.

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.850
<b><i>Himematsu</i></b>

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:21.210
I'm back.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:24.060
Great game!

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:25.480
Welcome back!

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:28.270
After you handed me the baton in first place,

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:31.580
I'm really sorry for ending up in second.

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:33.610
It's not a problem at all.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:35.490
Although, we got pretty 
nervous in the middle.

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:40.470
But somehow, I don't feel exactly satisfied.

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:41.920
What do you mean?

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:44.800
Suehara-chan, good job!

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:49.050
Huh? What's the matter?

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:50.430
Don't tell me...

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:52.800
It's the records from the 
individual tournament, right?

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:55.170
Captain, you told me to do that, right?

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:57.720
To look at play records of the opponent's losses.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:01.330
Yeah, I mean, if you want to win, 
you can learn the most

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:03.850
from seeing what made them lose.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:08.110
But Miyanaga Saki has had matches 
where she neither won nor lost.

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:11.310
In the individual tournament at the regionals,

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:14.110
she continuously had a plus-minus 0 score.

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:16.860
Then, in the fifth players' match just now...

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:21.870
Say the first and second half were each 
regular 25,000 point East-South matches.

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:25.120
That means she had two 
plus-minus 0 matches in a row!

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:27.870
Yet she still ended in first place!

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:31.640
Kyouko...

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:37.130
Suehara-chan.

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:41.140
Do you want to get stronger than that girl?

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:45.080
Stronger?

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:46.010
Yes.

00:09:46.010 --> 00:09:48.650
You want to become 
stronger than her, right?

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:50.370
W-Well, sure...

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:55.990
If that's the case, we need to start...

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:01.790
with your appearance!

00:10:05.260 --> 00:10:05.980
Huh?

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:08.140
Can you please take this seriously?

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:11.670
But I'm being totally serious!

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:15.340
If you change how you look, 
that will change how you feel,

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:18.180
and it might help you show 
a different side of yourself.

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:21.830
I know you're a strong person to begin with.

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:23.440
That's...

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:25.640
I don't know what you're talking about!

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:31.450
I think I also underestimated 
Miyanaga Saki-chan a little.

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:34.440
That's why I called someone new!

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:47.030
Good morning.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:48.540
Mahjong Pro
 Kainou Yoshiko

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:48.580
Pro player Kainou!

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:49.950
It's evening...

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:52.650
This is amazing! Our first meeting 
with a top pro in ages!

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:54.290
How wonderful!

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:57.560
Did you see Miyanaga Saki-chan back there?

00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:58.390
Yes.

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:05.010
I sensed it directly in the hall,
 but she's a real monster.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:07.160
If she had been in the first round match,

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:09.280
I could have given you some advice.

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:10.580
Pro player Kainou?

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:11.230
Yes?

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:15.270
Were you really a mercenary 
shaman in the Middle East?

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:19.610
I heard you won a yakuman summoning 
the powers of King Solomon!

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:22.680
No, no. No way, no way.

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:26.450
So Kainou-chan, to get right to the point...

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:28.100
No problem.

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:30.020
Great!

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:34.200
I invited about twenty more 
awesome people to come over here.

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:38.020
We'll be having practice 
matches until tomorrow evening.

00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:43.430
We'll have Kainou-chan do something 
similar to what Miyanaga Saki-chan does.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:46.430
Are these people different from 
the fifteen who were here

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:47.970
yesterday and the day before?

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:52.120
I tuned the list according to our 
opponents in the semifinals.

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:53.830
You can look forward to it!

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:58.070
Thanks for giving my cousin Haru a good game.

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:01.570
That shrine priestess is your cousin?

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:03.250
How about that.

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:05.930
<i>I guess it's like me and Hiroko.</i>

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:09.330
So, about the semifinals 
the day after tomorrow.

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:12.620
Zenno-san is coming to watch.

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:14.550
Really?

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:17.840
<i>Is she serious?</i>

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:23.680
<i>I can't afford to lose, then!</i>

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:27.930
<b>Eisui Girls'</b>

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:32.430
The cleansing is done.

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:34.600
Thank you. Sorry for the hassle.

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:37.020
Not at all. I'm used to it.

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:50.620
Good job.

00:12:51.070 --> 00:12:52.890
Are you all right?

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:53.890
Yes.

00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:58.750
I am so sorry about today.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.340
I was of no help.

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:03.740
We could say the same.

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:06.540
If only I had done my job better...

00:13:06.540 --> 00:13:09.190
It's not your fault, Princess.

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:15.480
Actually, the order in which 
the gods descend is set.

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:17.620
Like a god rotation?

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:18.810
That's right.

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:21.900
We arranged it so that weaker gods 
would come in the second round match,

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:28.060
and stronger gods from the semifinals 
onward, but that strategy backfired.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:32.050
I guess underestimating is never wise.

00:13:32.050 --> 00:13:35.490
It's hard to play against 
girls who use powers that are

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:37.080
suited for mahjong.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:41.900
Concentrating our powers into 
such a small space is really difficult.

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:44.460
All of this can be seen as training, though.

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:48.720
But that means the Princess will only have

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:51.510
strong gods during the individual tournament.

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:53.600
I hope it'll be enough to get her to the finals.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:56.890
They won't descend into her unless 
her opponents are very strong,

00:13:56.890 --> 00:13:58.560
so it's hard to say.

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:01.730
The soba is here!

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:05.320
I was starving!

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:09.200
Well, let's eat.

00:14:17.730 --> 00:14:19.830
The individual tournament is in five days.

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:21.960
So we have some free time now.

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:23.880
Yeah...

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:27.110
Well then.

00:14:27.110 --> 00:14:28.870
Since they're in the individual tournament,

00:14:28.870 --> 00:14:32.120
let's leave Komaki-chan and 
Hatsumi-chan here in Tokyo

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:35.350
and go swim in the ocean or visit a hot spring!

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:40.210
But I want to go, too!

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:41.100
I want to go.

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:42.880
Great idea!

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:45.530
We can ask Akise-chan from the 
middle school to come, too!

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:48.900
Am I the only one of the six 
female sages being left out?

00:14:49.890 --> 00:14:52.770
But we can't leave Komaki-chan alone,

00:14:52.770 --> 00:14:55.500
and there's some time until 
the individual tournament.

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:57.500
Let's all go together, after all.

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:59.120
Oh, good!

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:01.500
If we're talking swimming, just leave it to me!

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:03.250
Whee!

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:05.850
<i>Four days off...</i>

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:21.140
Komaki-chan!

00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:22.270
Y-Yes?

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:24.450
You were asleep, weren't you?

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:27.240
Komaki-chan, I have a favor to ask.

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:31.710
A girl from Iwate asked 
me for your autograph.

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:33.160
Could you write one for her?

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:35.040
My autograph?

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:36.060
Yes.

00:15:38.340 --> 00:15:40.270
"To Toyone-chan," please.

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:42.790
That's Toyone-chan, written with 
the characters "rich" and "sound."

00:15:43.220 --> 00:15:44.630
Oh, her?

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:56.680
<b>Miyamori Girls'</b>

00:15:57.220 --> 00:15:59.430
I'm back!

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:04.550
Toyone...

00:16:04.550 --> 00:16:06.020
Welcome back.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:09.150
I got all these autographs!

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:12.090
First, the other three girls 
from the fifth players' match...

00:16:12.090 --> 00:16:15.560
And even though I asked so shamelessly,

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:19.730
they said they'd get me autographs 
from Haramura-san and Jindai-san, too!

00:16:19.730 --> 00:16:21.860
I'm so happy!

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:24.060
Toyone?

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:29.670
I had the chance to come 
to this festival with all of you.

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:32.920
I got to be here with you this summer.

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:35.930
This will be a memento

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:39.160
of those precious memories.

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:42.170
Toyone!

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:51.560
<i>What a shame.</i>

00:16:51.560 --> 00:16:54.620
<i>I never thought we wouldn't 
even get into the top eight.</i>

00:16:56.560 --> 00:16:58.780
Yes, come in.

00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:00.590
Excuse me...

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:08.470
We came to bring the autograph 
board you had asked for.

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:11.430
Jindai-san?!

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:12.300
You came yourself?!

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:14.230
It's nice to meet you.

00:17:17.110 --> 00:17:19.600
Will this be all right?

00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:24.070
It's amazing, just amazing!

00:17:24.070 --> 00:17:25.850
I will treasure it!

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:27.430
I'm glad to hear it.

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:30.270
What is that?

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:31.980
You mean this?

00:17:32.520 --> 00:17:33.760
It's an inner tube!

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:35.700
I gathered that.

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:38.500
We have a few days before the

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:41.490
individual tournament, so we 
decided to go to the ocean.

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:44.160
I worked hard to blow it up myself.

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:45.960
But there is no ocean around here!

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:48.120
The ocean... sounds nice.

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:50.120
I love the ocean!

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:51.960
Why don't you all go as well?

00:17:52.310 --> 00:17:56.050
If your schedule allows it, 
would you like to come with us?

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:57.630
If we're not intruding...

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:59.340
Whoa! It's not a bother for you?!

00:17:58.030 --> 00:17:59.160
Whoa!

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:02.600
The players playing in 
the individual tournament

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:04.730
should not play against each other.

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:05.980
It's already decided?

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:08.460
Where do you plan to visit the ocean?

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:11.440
We thought of going to the beach 
of the sacred Kirishima village.

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:12.380
Kirishima?!

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:14.480
You're going too, right, Toyone?

00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:16.740
Yeah!

00:18:19.730 --> 00:18:20.990
I'm back!

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:23.990
Saki-chan?!

00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:27.190
Welcome back. Are you all right?

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:28.760
Ow...

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:31.280
Thank goodness, the autograph board is safe.

00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:32.250
Autograph board?

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.800
You did it, Saki! You're amazing!

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:37.980
Thanks, Kyou-chan.

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:41.330
I got a little lost after I left the interview.

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:43.800
You were barely able to speak!

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:44.810
Oh, that reminds me.

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:48.840
Anetai-san asked me to get 
your autograph, Nodoka-chan.

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:49.590
What?

00:18:49.590 --> 00:18:51.770
But I don't have an autograph.

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:55.400
Then just write your name normally.

00:18:56.600 --> 00:18:59.720
I thought autographs were 
supposed to be all squiggly.

00:18:59.720 --> 00:19:03.350
Well, let's see! What does 
Nodo-chan's autograph look like?

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:04.780
In any case...

00:19:05.680 --> 00:19:08.710
Your way of winning never ceases 
to amaze me. Here you go.

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:10.770
Thanks...

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:15.800
I'm sorry, Captain.

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:16.840
Huh?

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:18.760
I tried to play like you told me to.

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:23.000
Like I only had 1,000 points left.

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:28.060
But playing against those three girls, 
that simply wasn't possible...

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:29.730
All I could see was the

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:33.560
playing style I'm most used to, 
from back when I was a kid.

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:38.160
I tried, but that was all I could do.

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:41.320
And worse, the toughest player 
remained in the top two...

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:43.200
<i>Himematsu!</i>

00:19:43.730 --> 00:19:47.080
If I play her again, I don't think I can win.

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:52.020
Since you kept your socks on,

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:53.770
I thought you still had plenty of leeway.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.970
I forgot all about that!

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:00.900
<i>This looks like it'll be a bit of an issue.</i>

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:05.220
This is the Mahjong Inter-high Summary!

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:07.240
After the sixth day of competition,

00:20:07.240 --> 00:20:09.760
the top eight schools have been decided!

00:20:09.760 --> 00:20:11.730
Among them, there are three seed schools

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:14.730
and two schools making their first appearance.

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:16.900
In the semifinals beginning tomorrow,

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:19.950
the four schools that will move on 
to the finals will be determined.

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:19.930
Hayarin!

00:20:19.930 --> 00:20:21.670
I wonder if Achiga will be there?

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:23.240
After seeing the matches up to today,

00:20:21.670 --> 00:20:23.240
This pro's tough.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:26.410
did any particular school 
make an impression on you?

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:28.740
I don't know about a favorite...

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:28.740
Shiraitodai (West Tokyo)                                                         Kiyosumi (Nagano)
 Shindouji Girls' (Fukuoka)                                             Himematsu (South Osaka)
 Achiga Girls' (Nara)                                                        Usuzan (South Hokkaido)
 Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)                                     Rinkai Girls' (East Tokyo)

00:20:29.060 --> 00:20:32.410
But the team I want to fight the least is

00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:37.290
Usuzan High School, who's making 
their first appearance this year.

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:38.130
Big Sister of the Tiles

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:48.090
We came here with the 
intention of winning.

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:50.430
Any one of those schools could've won.

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:52.310
It was a good game.

00:20:54.960 --> 00:21:00.010
I've known those girls less than a year.

00:21:00.010 --> 00:21:01.820
But now...

00:21:03.810 --> 00:21:05.680
I wish I could have 
shown them what's ahead,

00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:08.600
even for just a tiny bit.

00:22:40.510 --> 00:22:42.060
I should go soon.

00:22:42.060 --> 00:22:45.300
You must have a lot of preparations 
to make for tomorrow!

00:22:45.650 --> 00:22:48.950
I've already prepared all that I can.

00:22:49.380 --> 00:22:51.300
Now all that's left is to believe in those girls

00:22:51.840 --> 00:22:53.260
and take on the semifinals!

00:22:55.230 --> 00:22:56.960
Is that so?

00:22:56.960 --> 00:23:00.190
You have really grown into 
your role as a coach.

00:23:00.700 --> 00:23:02.880
So, as for what we talked about yesterday...

00:23:02.880 --> 00:23:03.560
Yes.

00:23:03.560 --> 00:23:05.410
I'm honored, but...

00:23:24.870 --> 00:23:26.040
A dream?

00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:49.780
<b>Next time:</b>

00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:49.780
<b>Old Friends</b>

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:42.120
You're all here...

00:23:42.120 --> 00:23:44.690
Then it's off to the semifinals!

00:23:49.780 --> 00:24:00.000
<b>Watch
Next
Time</b>
